::zendesk ns
meta {
    doc: """
    Zendesk Support API bindings.

    - `::zendesk::tickets` creates, reads, updates, comments on, merges and
      tags tickets, lists ticket fields and satisfaction ratings, and runs
      the cursor-based incremental ticket export
    - `::zendesk::users` and `::zendesk::organizations` look up and manage
      requesters and their companies
    - `::zendesk::views` and `::zendesk::macros` work the queues agents
      use: execute a view, preview or apply a macro
    - `::zendesk::search` runs the search API (with its 1,000-result cap)
      and the cursor-based search export
    - `::zendesk::side-conversations` starts and replies to side
      conversations
    - `::zendesk::webhooks` verifies `X-Zendesk-Webhook-Signature`
    - `::zendesk::api` holds the transport, cursor pagination, and the
      `request` escape hatch

    **Setup**: context variables:
    - `zendesk.subdomain`: `acme` or `acme.zendesk.com`
    - API token auth: `zendesk.email` (the agent or admin the token acts
      as) and `zendesk.api.token` (Admin Center → Apps and integrations →
      APIs → Zendesk API)
    - or OAuth: `zendesk.oauth.token`, a Bearer access token (wins when
      both are set)

    Every API-calling function also takes a trailing `opts` Map for
    per-call credentials; see `::zendesk::api`.

    **Quick start**

    ```hot
    ::tickets ::zendesk::tickets

    urgent ::zendesk::search/search("type:ticket status:open priority:urgent")

    ticket ::tickets/create-ticket("Login page down", "Customers report 500s on /login.", {priority: "urgent"})
    ::tickets/add-comment(ticket.ticket.id, "Deployed a rollback; monitoring.", false)
    ```
    """
}

// Cursor pagination page size used by the list helpers; 100 is the
// maximum most Zendesk list endpoints accept.
DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE 100
